# Local settings. `just` loads a `.env` beside the justfile into every recipe
# (`set dotenv-load`), and git ignores it. Copy this file to `.env` and uncomment
# what you need; a variable already set in your shell wins over the file.
# `just where` prints what the recipes will use.

# --- The lakehouse's Parquet in an S3-compatible bucket (docs/WAREHOUSE.md) ---
#
# Unset, the Parquet sits under $LAKEHOUSE_DIR/data/, beside the catalog. Set, it
# goes to this bucket and prefix; the catalog stays a local file either way.
#
# - Choose before the first `just ingest`: the catalog records its data path and
#   refuses any other, so switching an existing landing zone is not a toggle.
# - `just export-data` and `just restore-history` refuse while it is set. The
#   release is built from a landing zone on disk.
#
# The values below match the SeaweedFS container docs/WAREHOUSE.md starts.
#LAKEHOUSE_DATA_PATH=s3://lake/modern-data-stack/
# The store's URL, scheme included: http:// turns TLS off, https:// keeps it.
#LAKEHOUSE_S3_ENDPOINT=http://127.0.0.1:8333
#AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=test
#AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=testtest
# Optional. Most S3-compatible stores ignore the region, but a request signature
# still names one.
#AWS_REGION=us-east-1
